Batch 21 arm: K10-O1 — the CEM force formula on trinity's OWN ionisation front.
Apply to BASE_SHA in a clean worktree via run_arms.sh; never on a working main
checkout. Supersedes k10_arm.patch (Batch 18), which solved its own front and was
measured OUTSIDE the neutral shell on 18/18 B3M momentum rows and outside the cloud
on 100% of driving rows. Maintainer chose O1 on 2026-08-29.

  drive = P_conf * (R_IF/R2)^2,  R_IF read verbatim from ShellProperties.R_IF

`_k10_front_radius` is DELETED, which removes by construction: the thin-dust guard that
tested the wrong quantity and never fired, the float64 bracket failure (unhandled
ValueError / silently 8.9%-wrong root at low metallicity), and the ZeroDivisionError /
OverflowError paths on extreme Eb. Dust is inherited from the shell solve's own ODE.

